                "event": "Beach Hazards Statement",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
                "headline": "Beach Hazards Statement issued October 4 at 1:26PM PDT until October 9 at 11:00PM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Dangerous rip currents and breaking waves are expected\ndue to elevated surf of 3 to 6 feet. Abnormally high morning\nand evening tides of 6.5 to 7 ft is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Catalina and Santa Barbara Islands, Ventura County\nBeaches, Malibu Coast and Los Angeles County Beaches. Most\nsusceptible areas will be Long Beach and Avalon Harbor Tuesday\nand Wednesday. Then, Mailbu to Ventura Wednesday through\nFriday.\n\n* WHEN...From Tuesday afternoon through Friday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...There is an increased risk of ocean drowning. Rip\ncurrents can pull swimmers and surfers out to sea. Waves can\nwash people off beaches and rocks, and capsize small boats\nnearshore. Moderate flooding of sea water is possibly over\nsome vulnerable low-lying coastal areas, especially around the\nmorning and evening high tides, including over beach parking\nlots, bike paths, and harbor walkways. Moderate beach erosion\nis possible to likely.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...There is a moderate chance that an\nupgrade to Coastal Flood Advisory and/or High Surf Advisory\nwill be needed. These products will likely need to be extended\ninto the weekend.",
                "instruction": "Remain out of the water due to hazardous swimming conditions, or\nstay near occupied lifeguard towers. Rock jetties can be deadly\nin such conditions, stay off the rocks.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
